-- title:
--   Abel's theorem for X_H(M): unitary multiplier and period reciprocity
-- statement:
--   Fix $M\ge 1$ and a subgroup $H\le(\mathbb Z/M)^\times$, and let $\Gamma=$ [`CohCarrier.GammaH M H`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L133) be the image in $SL(2,\mathbb Z)$ of the subgroup of $\Gamma_0(M)$ on which the homomorphism `gamma0Units M` (the unit class of the lower-right entry mod $M$) takes values in $H$. Let $D$ be a complex place dictionary for $\Gamma$ and the field [`ModularCurve.xHFunctionField M H`](def/ModularCurve_XH.html#L79), that is: a map $\mathrm{pt}:\mathfrak H\to$ places of the base-changed function field, a ramification function $e:\mathfrak H\to\mathbb N$ with $e_\tau>0$, invariance $\mathrm{pt}(\gamma\tau)=\mathrm{pt}(\tau)$ for $\gamma\in\Gamma$, the description of the valuation subring of $\mathrm{pt}(\tau)$ as those $x$ whose realisation `realizeOf` is bounded near $\tau$, and $\mathrm{ord}_\tau$ of the realisation of $x\ne 0$ equal to $e_\tau\cdot\mathrm{ord}_{\mathrm{pt}(\tau)}(x)$. Let $c:\mathfrak H\to\mathbb Z$ be finitely supported and assume the pushforward divisor $\tilde c=$ `Finsupp.mapDomain D.pt c` has degree $0$. Then there are $F:\mathfrak H\to\mathbb C$, $\chi:\Gamma\to\mathbb C$ and a weight-$2$ cusp form $f$ for $\Gamma$ such that: $z\mapsto F(\mathrm{ofComplex}\,z)$ is meromorphic at every $\tau\in\mathfrak H$; $F(\gamma\tau)=\chi(\gamma)F(\tau)$ for $\gamma\in\Gamma$; $\lVert\chi(\gamma)\rVert=1$; for each $\sigma\in SL(2,\mathbb Z)$ the function $\tau\mapsto F(\sigma\tau)$ tends to a nonzero limit as $\operatorname{Im}\tau\to\infty$; the meromorphic order of $F$ at $\tau$ equals $e_\tau\cdot\tilde c(\mathrm{pt}(\tau))$; $\chi(\gamma)=\exp\bigl(2\pi i\,\operatorname{Re}(\mathrm{periodOf}\,\Gamma\,\gamma\,f)\bigr)$, where $\mathrm{periodOf}\,\Gamma\,\gamma$ is the functional $h\mapsto\int_i^{\gamma i}h$ along the segment path; and finally there is $\Lambda$ in the period lattice [`ModularCurve.periodLatticeOf Γ`](def/ModularCurve_PeriodOf.html#L65) (the $\mathbb Z$-span of these functionals inside the $\mathbb C$-dual of weight-$2$ cusp forms) with $$\sum_\tau c(\tau)\,\bigl(\textstyle\int_i^{\tau}g\bigr)+i\int_{\mathcal F(\Gamma\sqcup\langle-1\rangle)}\mathrm{petersson}\,2\,f\,g\;=\;\Lambda(g)$$ for every weight-$2$ cusp form $g$ for $\Gamma$, the integral being over [`FLT.Gamma0FundamentalSet.gammaFundamentalSet`](def/AutomorphicForm_Gamma0FundamentalSet.html#L13) of the subgroup generated by $\Gamma$ and $-1$, namely the union of the $SL(2,\mathbb Z)$-coset translates of the standard fundamental domain.
--
--   This is the sufficiency half of Abel's theorem on the modular curve $X_H(M)$: a degree-zero divisor is realised as the order divisor of a function with unimodular multiplier system, the multiplier being the exponential of the real part of a period of an associated weight-$2$ cusp form, together with Riemann's bilinear relation expressing the Abel–Jacobi functional plus $i$ times the Petersson pairing against $f$ as a lattice point. It is used by [`ModularCurve.ComplexPlaceDictionaryOf.multiplier_eq_one_of_norm_eq_one_of_abelJacobi_mem_periodLatticeOf_gammaH`](thm.html#ModularCurve.ComplexPlaceDictionaryOf.multiplier_eq_one_of_norm_eq_one_of_abelJacobi_mem_periodLatticeOf_gammaH), where the multiplier is forced to be trivial so that $F$ descends to a function on the curve.
